    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/972456?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Robot Learning for Manipulation",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in Robot Learning for Manipulation Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in Robot Learning for Manipulation KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description The postdoctoral researcher will work on robot learning for manipulation, exploring state-of-the-art Vision–Language–Action (VLA) models for tabletop, mobile, or dexterous manipulation. A key focus is leveraging whole-body motion and/or dexterous, multi-fingered hands to improve perception and control, enabling robots to solve complex, contact-rich tasks that require coordinated base, arm, and hand behaviors in dynamic environments. We seek candidates with a strong background in robotics and machine learning, and demonstrated experience in at least two of the following areas: deep learning, reinforcement learning, imitation learning, robot perception, navigation, grasping, and dexterous or mobile manipulation. Experience in any of the following is especially valued: whole-body control, humanoid or multi-DOF platforms, multi-fingered hands, tactile sensing, or learning-based manipulation in simulation and/or on real systems. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. Research expertise in machine learning/robotics. Documented strong programming skills. The candidate should have an outstanding research and publication list. You have well developed analytical and problem-solving skills. The candidate should have very good knowledge of the English language, such as written and oral skills since communication is essential of this role. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline You have good pedagogical ability. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. You are independent in your work and have no problem collaborating with others. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 2 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3257 Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Contact Danica Kragic Jensfelt dani@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/974287?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in sustainable generative artificial intelligence for media",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in sustainable generative artificial intelligence for media Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in sustainable generative artificial intelligence for media KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description The five-year research project FrugalAI is exploring the impacts of using generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) for the creation of media content. Current genAI models, used for generating music, images, text, and other media, rely on vast data sets and require significant computational resources. Training genAI models and employing them on a global scale contributes to substantial energy consumption, resource depletion, and increased carbon emissions, exacerbating environmental harm. Our project aims to develop and promote an innovative, sustainable alternative to existing large and commercial genAI systems. It aims to reduce the environmental footprint of genAI technologies while fostering positive social impacts by prioritizing small, ethically sourced data sets, local models and compute, and encouraging sustainable behavior among users. The research and development conducted in the project can be regarded as situated within the area of human-centered AI. FrugalAI has the following objectives: Estimate the environmental impact of current big-data genAI. Construct a set of open-source frugal genAI tools based on small, ethical data. Map the impact on social sustainability that emerges from using frugal genAI. Compare the environmental impact of these tools with big-data genAI tools. Propose and apply evaluation metrics that consider resource use. Investigate implications for other genAI applications (e.g., image generation). The postdoctoral researcher, having a background related to HCI and machine learning, will contribute to all objectives over a period of two years at 100% time. Working with a diverse team of engineers, musicologists, and designers, the job will include the following tasks: Contribute to the development of an interactive online broadcasting environment (a prototype is “Stochastic Pirate Radio” KSPR) by designing and maintaining project software, and developing pipelines for creating media programs and the automated monitoring for offensive content, and estimating and tracking energy usage. Research and develop frugal AI principles to reduce model sizes, data, and computation using the state of the art in machine learning. Develop a multi-objective metric of genAI sustainability (environmental, economic, sociocultural), building from C. Douwes, On the Environmental Impact of Deep Generative Models for Audio , Doctoral dissertation, Sorbonne Université 2023). Help organize and run workshops with team members For more information, contact Bob L. T. Sturm ( bobs@kth.se ). Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. The working language of the project is English, so you should have fluency in English. You have a background related to HCI and machine learning As a person you have collaborative abilities Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality It’s commendable if you can work independently Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Cover letter presenting how your background aligns with the tasks of this position, and your interest in the overall project. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3304 Published 01.Oct.2026 Last application date 05.Nov.2026 Contact Bob Sturm bobs@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/925980?l=en": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Environmental impact analysis",
      "description": "KTH | Associate Professor in Environmental impact analysis Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Associate Professor in Environmental impact analysis School of Architecture and Built Environment at KTH Subject field Environmental impact analysis Subject description The subject environmental impact analysis encompasses theoretical, methodological, and applied research for environmental assessment of projects, plans, and programs. Its core focus is on developing and critically examining how environmental aspects are integrated into planning and decision-making processes to promote sustainable development, with attention to both content and practical application. The subject also includes analysis of how knowledge, methods, and tools are used at various stages of the process, and how these contribute to and influence decision-making, implementation, and follow-up. By employing a range of qualitative and quantitative methods for environmental systems analysis and decision support, the field makes ecological, climate-related, and other sustainability-critical knowledge available for planning purposes. The research is conducted within a context where both Swedish and international perspectives are central. Collaboration with the public sector and the business community is crucial for its relevance and implementation. With an increasing focus on emerging sustainability challenges, such as climate adaptation, digitalization, circular solutions, and equity, the field contributes to the development of future practice, integrated planning processes, and the knowledge required for sustainable urban and regional development. Duties Duties include teaching, course development, and examination at both undergraduate and advanced levels within the subject area and related fields. The associate professor is expected to actively contribute to the development of courses and degree programs at the department and to provide relevant links to society for the student groups involved. It is also crucial that teaching is closely linked to current research to foster a research-integrated educational environment. Teaching, including supervision of degree projects, is conducted in both Swedish and English. Initially, it accounts for approximately 50% of the position but is subject to adjustment based on the department's needs. Administrative and supervisory tasks related to teaching may also be included. Research duties involve conducting independent research within the subject area and actively seeking and securing external research funding. The associate professor is expected to contribute to the department’s development and the academic environment by initiating and participating in research collaborations with other research groups within the department and across KTH. Collaboration with external stakeholders, nationally and internationally, as well as with industry and the public sector, is a vital component in grounding, developing, and realizing the impact of the research. The associate professor is expected to establish and develop independent and internationally recognized research. Duties also include seeking external funding for, and supervising, doctoral students and postdoctoral researchers. The position also entails active participation in academic activities at the department, the school, and KTH, including undertaking positions of trust as well as administrative and leadership roles within the department. The associate professor is also expected to contribute to the department's vision of playing a leading role in achieving KTH's goals regarding sustainable development and climate impact. Eligibility Those eligible to be employed as associate professor are persons who have: 1.    completed a doctorate or possess equivalent scientific expertise or some other professional expertise that is of significance with regard to the subject content of the employment and the duties that are required of the employment, and 2.    demonstrated pedagogical expertise. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria for appointment as an associate professor at KTH shall be the degree of expertise required as a qualification for employment. In addition, the assessment criteria stated in the KTH appointments procedure, section 1.2., apply in relation to the employment profile laid down. Of highest importance is that the applicant has •    scientific expertise in environmental impact analysis •    pedagogical expertise in environmental impact analysis, demonstrated through, among other things, experience of individual supervision at both undergraduate and doctoral levels •    the ability to work within the field in both a Swedish and an international context •    the ability to teach in Swedish Of second highest importance that the applicant has •    the ability to collaborate •    the ability to engage with the surrounding community for mutual exchange and to have worked to ensure that the knowledge and expertise available at the university benefit society It is also important that the applicant has •    expertise in developing and leading activities and staff. For that purpose, the individual is to be knowledgeable about diversity and equal opportunity issues, particularly gender equality. •    administrative expertise Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives can be found at KTH's webpage . Application Your application should follow KTH's CV template for employment of teachers . It is the responsibility of the applicant to ensure that the application is complete according to the requirements in the ad and CV template. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply to this position online. For more information regarding KTH's assessement, see Appointments procedure at the Royal Institute of Technology Other For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process please read here. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. Guidance on relocating and settling in at KTH and in Sweden. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly pay Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2126 Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 10.Nov.2026 Contact Anna Björklund annab@kth.se Maria Malmström malmstro@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    }
